# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL. A session transcribes with no keys at all:
# Deiko's relay handles it, and failing that the on-device recogniser produces
# both the words and their timings. These are for running against your own
# accounts instead.

# Sarvam — the words themselves. Set this and your narration audio goes
# straight to Sarvam with your key and never reaches Deiko's servers (filing a
# brief into its task still sends what you said through the relay). Word TIMINGS always come
# from on-device Apple Speech, with or without this.
SARVAM_API_KEY=

# Groq — the orb's three-line reading of a session. Without it (and without the
# relay) the orb simply shows the counts instead. Only the NARRATION is ever
# sent here — never referent text, OCR, window titles, or crops.
# See scripts/summarize.mjs. Filing a brief into its task is separate and still
# goes through Deiko's relay, key or no key — see scripts/classify.mjs.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# ── What `make relay-deploy` needs (names only; values live in .env) ─────────
#
# The deploy refuses to run without a Groq key, a playground secret and one
# classifier key, because a deploy that silently drops one of these takes a
# route down for everybody. The relay reads them by these names.
#
# DEIKO_PLAYGROUND_SECRET   signs the website playground's tickets
# DEIKO_PLAYGROUND_ORIGINS  comma-separated origins allowed to use the playground
#                           (production: https://deiko.app,https://www.deiko.app —
#                           drop localhost before launch)
# One classifier key, for /v1/classify (task filing), in order of preference:
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY          TypeSafe direct
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY        Vercel AI Gateway
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY        OpenRouter
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID + CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN   Cloudflare Workers AI
# DEIKO_CLASSIFIES_PER_DAY  optional daily ceiling for /v1/classify

# Deiko's relay — the default for anyone who sets neither key above. Normally
# baked into the app; set here to test against a local server:
#   node services/relay/server.mjs
# See services/relay/README.md.
# DEIKO_RELAY_URL=http://localhost:8787

# Keep the session's audio after the brief is made. Off by default — the
# recording is deleted the moment it has been used. Worth turning on when
# diagnosing a transcription problem, because the WAV is the only evidence of
# what the microphone actually heard.
# DEIKO_KEEP_AUDIO=1

# ── What the build stamps into the app bundle ───────────────────────────────
#
# `make install` and `make bundle` read these from here when they are not given
# on the command line. They exist because a plain `make install` used to stamp
# them EMPTY over a previously-correct build: the app then transcribed every
# session on-device while reporting `degraded: false`, and the mangled words
# read as a broken aligner rather than a missing relay.
#
# An explicit empty still works and still means it — `make install RELAY_URL=`
# builds a deliberately relay-less app. `make release` ignores this file and
# requires both URLs on the command line, because a release bakes them into a
# plist that can never be corrected remotely.
RELAY_URL=
SITE_URL=
SUPPORT_EMAIL=
BUY_URL=
